#exam-pointer(title: "High-Yield Memory Hooks for CUET 2027 Business Studies Unit 3")[
  Keep these fundamental conceptual anchors primed during the exam:
  - *Specific vs General Forces:* Specific forces (investors, customers, competitors, suppliers) directly affect a single enterprise; General forces (economic, social, political, legal, technological) affect all firms in the industry broadly.
  - *Relativity:* The environment differs across countries and regions (e.g., saree demand high in India, absent in Germany).
  - *First Mover Advantage vs Early Warning Signal:* Opportunities enable first-mover gains (Maruti); Threats trigger early warnings to build defenses.
  - *Political vs Legal:* Government stability, ruling party ideology, and "Make in India" campaigns = Political; Acts of Parliament, court judgments, and mandatory warning labels = Legal.
  - *Seller's vs Buyer's Market:* Pre-1991 = Seller's market (shortages, firm dictated terms); Post-1991 = Buyer's market (demanding consumers, market orientation).
  - *De-licensing Exceptions:* Exactly 6 strategic/hazardous industries still require compulsory licensing.
  - *Demonetisation Metric:* Approximately 86% of currency in circulation was withdrawn overnight; it was a tax administration and formalization measure.
]

